 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Yaskawa_Solectria_PVI_50_100_KW_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Solectria PVI 50-100 kW Modbus map (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/solectriapvi50100kw.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "Only 72 of the 77 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
 ],
